; Project-level instrumentation aliases — the two workflows windtrap
; tells its users to adopt, adopted here. Both are opt-in: neither is
; attached to @default or @runtest, and a plain `dune runtest` stays
; uninstrumented, zero-overhead and free of coverage and mutation output.
;
;   dune build @cover  --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.coverage
;   dune build @mutate --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.mutate
;
; Why an alias and not a script: `.coverage` and `.mutants` files are
; written by test executables at exit and are not declarable dependencies,
; so nothing can express "after every suite has run". (alias_rec runtest)
; forces every stanza in the tree up to date first, and (universe) makes
; the milliseconds-cheap aggregate re-run on every build — without it the
; action caches against nothing and silently goes stale. This is the
; shape examples/09-coverage-aggregation documents, one level up.
;
; The backend spelled here is `ppx_windtrap.coverage`, not the
; `ppx_windtrap` the manual shows users: only the former keeps the
; windtrap core out of an instrumented library's closure, and lib/ — the
; core itself — cannot use the latter at all. See ppx/coverage/dune.

; --min 87 is the measured baseline (89.5% at the time of writing) less a
; couple of points of headroom, not a round number picked in advance. It
; ratchets: raise it when the margin is comfortable, and never lower it to
; make a red build green. The remaining gap is not all reachable —
; mutate_loop's Windows-decline paths and capture's C-stub error branches
; cannot run in a green suite — so chase the branches the report names,
; not the percentage.

(rule
 (alias cover)
 (deps
  (alias_rec runtest)
  (universe))
 (action
  (run %{bin:windtrap} coverage --min 87)))

; Mutation has no gate and deliberately never will (Law 16e): the
; equivalent-mutant rate is a prediction until it is measured, so a
; survivor is a reading list, not a build failure.

(rule
 (alias mutate)
 (deps
  (alias_rec runtest)
  (universe))
 (action
  (run %{bin:windtrap} mutate)))
